  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Definitions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "WHO reports that levodopa/carbidopa is not accessible, available or affordable everywhere, particularly in low- and middle-income countries. (low confidence) (verified as of 2023-08-09)",
          "source": "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/parkinson-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:edf29ed1d8d9bd54458a5ddc9b89616fe4e2167ac1434b979613a9b2c2f609c8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:dca706e5db18b805fe164e618dbbf6e17c6e5e00bdcfe9d2b17633f45a8084df"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Measurements and reference values",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Fothergill-Misbah and colleagues found that 81% (38/47) of countries in the WHO African Region included levodopa plus carbidopa or levodopa plus benserazide as a therapeutic alternative on national essential medicines lists, considering any formulation or strength. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-08-25)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12481222/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2ec45b84c1af783552077b142614355c599e6382bdf06de10b2d35f72e6cb11f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0078e725ef51869ea37d88c4ea1620e4eaba61da0cf2015871390204a569e92f",
            "ev:35f605af8382daa8b2a19ef807c224dc66a7cf6f1305531bba074015f5a3f836",
            "ev:b0bee6861f0feda2c1f7af07f8ea83750d1860a17ecc8d43d3a7924d5b4306ee"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Middle East physician survey reported levodopa availability of 98% among its participating countries. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13380763/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0b50d7cb749e229479e8111afda7c0693d024ba33f0823d8034c8be4f077563c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:799caa8063e28edfbd246fa596c1eaa3355b07f4555971481c58eefbe31623e1",
            "ev:b1afcd4bbd06e45006e673d9d657dadf734d0f9cc4404506f1593463f8eac957"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "WHO reports that global estimates in 2019 showed over 8.5 million individuals with Parkinson disease. (low confidence) (verified as of 2023-08-09)",
          "source": "https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/parkinson-disease",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0fb60e02e44bef1f68cfd06dc6f9814e6b7ee030b8693ac7c63d1f752c355c2f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:40363ab66295b41066b812b43f875865e7ec4e80de7510cfd3cfc8547a9eecdd"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Global Burden of Disease collaborators estimated 6·1 million individuals with Parkinson disease globally in 2016, with a 95% uncertainty interval of 5·0–7·3 million. (low confidence) (verified as of 2018-11-01)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6191528/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:90d4d4efbb42439bb8751f859cfdcb8a37927c631cd81d7aeb489abbca0a4452",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:65280d61375953d6fbedb732f7cf6ac0f8c4231c7c065ca01a425ee536f3c452"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Luo and colleagues report that 11.77 million people worldwide had Parkinson disease in 2021, using the Global Burden of Disease Study 2021. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-01-10)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11757241/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:46750c7ed5026fc3928446dbfd4bcc166d032ec108546a9cdb7e04bc6da74bb3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0222f551767787fccfea5ea394c3d20db45a0b8c853fadc9febd3ba5a79f4521",
            "ev:b470cf9b1cb5d290841aa735c72c2589bcf59318e1b1b2290b3ed972eca73a73"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The BMJ modelling study projects 25.2 million people living with Parkinson disease worldwide in 2050, with a 95% uncertainty interval of 21.7 to 30.1 million. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-03-05)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40044233/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ad8db40f74908fe26785c8baafd5f207a1862d6e42c6276c63fce0f4ade6861e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5b42977e3e00b8e0cf7f6960fb0352c74226be223664d44dfd8e449ce3d43d9e"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Yang and colleagues estimated the total economic burden of diagnosed Parkinson disease in the United States in 2017 at $51.9 billion. (low confidence) (verified as of 2020-07-09)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7347582/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:31fe99f9f984220757175a17511bdd9a78c39ccddcf50a08bb33333ccd2029ec",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:66b1315b22887c7828a4fdddfa5d385e7242183328c1d8096ea998b66d3c503b",
            "ev:7036a2c720023ac57fe6ef840f4d39b0322848256749d38ce31fd8be0ff347ef"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Yang and colleagues projected the total economic burden of Parkinson disease in the United States to surpass $79 billion by 2037. (low confidence) (verified as of 2020-07-09)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7347582/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:1a05ec2c88cff3bca84c43e3cbb93594c19e1813c81fda68577449d1d5a6e760",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:66b1315b22887c7828a4fdddfa5d385e7242183328c1d8096ea998b66d3c503b",
            "ev:e8060e7bd296b6a287834c3ef0e0f9a93872d1be772284597988634f1ef50cf0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Lewin Group report estimates a combined economic burden of Parkinson disease and atypical parkinsonism of $82.2 billion in the United States for 2024. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-02-17)",
          "source": "https://www.michaeljfox.org/sites/default/files/media/document/Economic%20Burden%20of%20Parkinson%E2%80%99s%20and%20Atypical%20Parkinsonism%20in%20the%20United%20States_0.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4a9d2a82d3094291a9e3b824245a7064166e93cb030b0b4eb8e4c06f1f6208c1",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6a04ac5b197ff4190d73d688849eab18495f4807e92697b8b1c5d9520ff240e0",
            "ev:a691422332eb059d2d40cfe6864db54deea6ad9bdef003f8bdf7f8ee867fdb45"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.parkinson.org/about-us/news/economic-burden-2024-report"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fothergill-Misbah and colleagues state that inclusion of Parkinson disease medicines in national essential medicines lists provides no guarantee of immediate access. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-08-25)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12481222/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5b1ac40b467f19ed3dba2f1c2f4e04b3bc6854a59d59abe7dbc5da68712ceea5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:35f605af8382daa8b2a19ef807c224dc66a7cf6f1305531bba074015f5a3f836",
            "ev:f6f75c93138478647fd8d701ed2528b1df99cc2734181e5f33c26ee6060258f8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "WHO’s technical-brief launch news states that globally the prevalence of Parkinson disease has doubled in the past 25 years. (low confidence) (verified as of 2022-06-14)",
          "source": "https://www.who.int/news/item/14-06-2022-launch-of-who-s-parkinson-disease-technical-brief",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:152f8cebbf8cab0ca8c59119faab665b45825f75a9a0643985737f8cea279af2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:d638c8b73a4497d4659a57c9176a4027fbcff6ee36abc50172c58a79a6c27418"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Lewin Group report defines PWPD/AP as people with Parkinson’s disease inclusive of atypical parkinsonism. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-02-17)",
          "source": "https://www.michaeljfox.org/sites/default/files/media/document/Economic%20Burden%20of%20Parkinson%E2%80%99s%20and%20Atypical%20Parkinsonism%20in%20the%20United%20States_0.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7e41d2c87fa37288c2bb285f4c6754898d07553b9837731d18e0ac20a9312958",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:53dea9a4de0370242e26d918f875d8635088518f92c849c5384c3f9c4a42fd60"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The Middle East survey authors caution that their data were physician-reported perceptions rather than objective verification, with potential reporting bias and failure to capture within-country variability. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-08)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13380763/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:949ed8e7adaf7998afd47698470004c6b5ed37f26993afde3e5bfed6b3e7b420",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3cf08b9db75c8152c3baac2de50d368ae40e16c1da4002e970e016c6c94a6131"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The nationwide Nigerian pharmacy survey found that only trihexyphenidyl tablets and biperiden injection were affordable under its study definition. (low confidence) (verified as of 2018-11-16)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6335528/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7538bf8e3ae96ad78819fe6afc44606bdd7e7f933d73dfe502a2ab7a28b701e2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3c9cfba3f9d7376610b23e5209c5bc7fec955b7fe157cda831bc5b16cc2f3f69",
            "ev:93b15a7e5d619741bfb0ebd1a5bd9f527a167da88edae66a80e6f1a9d81abace"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Parkinson’s Foundation states that annual costs surpassed the $79 billion previously projected for 2037, more than a decade early. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/about-us/news/economic-burden-2024-report",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:139fb506bd5318ef2abb05063c8aa028dc4452ffccccf6920a75c664d7eb79f4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
