      "documentConcept": "Global burden, economic cost and access to PD care",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:a76bacb72e8d2a3bc1f9353fd3430195f5d9c088b739df55d1c7366928320a36",
      "text": "This concept connects estimates of the global Parkinson disease burden with economic costs and access to treatment. WHO and Global Burden of Disease analyses describe substantial populations living with the condition; the BMJ study models future prevalence. The economic studies quantify societal costs in the United States, with the later report covering both Parkinson disease and atypical parkinsonism. WHO describes barriers to medicine access, while studies of African essential medicines lists, Nigerian pharmacies and Middle Eastern physicians examine different aspects of access. Listing a medicine does not guarantee access, and physician perceptions do not substitute for objectively verified availability. Estimates remain attributed to their own studies, populations and methods.",
